.TH ROJ 1 "0.1.0" "roj 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
roj \- the Kurdish solar calendar in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B roj
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B roj
shows and converts dates in the Kurdish solar calendar, with the Gregorian,
Persian (Jalali) and Islamic (Hijri) calendars beside it. It uses the same
engine as the Roj GNOME Shell extension (the tsroj library) and, when run with
\fBgjs\fR, the extension's settings.
.PP
Roj means both sun and day in Kurdish.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B today
Today in all four calendars. This is the default command.
.TP
.BR cal " [\fIYYYY-MM\fR]"
A Kurdish month as a grid, this month by default.
.TP
.BI convert " DATE"
Convert \fIDATE\fR (YYYY-MM-DD) between calendars.
.TP
.BI format " PATTERN"
Format a date with a strftime pattern, for example "%A %d %B %Y".
.TP
.BR events " [\fIDATE\fR]"
Events on a day (today by default), from the built-in Kurdish events, your
extension's event sources and any \fB\-\-file\fR.
.TP
.B months
The twelve Kurdish months of this year, with lengths and start dates.
.TP
.B tokens
Every pattern token with examples.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-locale " \fILANG\fR"
Date language: ckb (Sorani), kmr (Kurmanji), en, fa or ar.
.TP
.BI \-\-secondary " MODE"
Language of the other calendars: same, or native (Gregorian in English,
Persian in Persian, Islamic in Arabic).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-from " \fICALENDAR\fR"
Calendar of the input date: kurdish, gregorian, persian or islamic.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-to " \fICALENDAR\fR"
Output calendar.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-date " \fIDATE\fR"
Date used by \fBformat\fR and \fBevents\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-with " g,p,i"
Small Gregorian, Persian and Islamic day numbers in \fBcal\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-month
With \fBevents\fR: the whole Kurdish month.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
An extra JSON or .ics events file. Can be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-digits " SET"
native, latin, arabic or persian digits.
.TP
.BR \-\-era " solar|nineveh"
Kurdish year numbering: Persian year + 1321, or + 1233.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ezafe
Turn off the Sorani ezafe (ی).
.TP
.BI \-\-islamic\-offset " N"
Days added to the Islamic date, from -3 to 3.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.TP
.BR \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color
Force or disable colours.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Ignore the GNOME extension's settings.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
roj
roj cal \-\-with g
roj convert 2026\-06\-26
roj convert 2726\-01\-01 \-\-from kurdish \-\-to gregorian
roj format "%A %d %B %Y" \-\-locale kmr
roj events \-\-month \-\-file holidays.ics
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on an error such as an invalid date, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://0xdolan.github.io/roj/guide.html
